{"date": "2026-10-31", "post_id": 1506814, "title": "Night on a Spooky Planet", "permalink": "https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-31-night-on-a-spooky-planet/", "media_type": "image", "explanation": "<strong>Explanation:</strong> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/sinister-solar-system/\">What spooky planet is this?</a> Planet Earth on a dark and stormy night, of course. The ghostly scene was <a href=\"https://twanight.org/gallery/night-on-a-spooky-planet/\">photographed at Hverir</a>, a geothermally active area found along northeastern Iceland's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krafla\">volcanic landscape</a>. Triggered by <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/sun/solar-storms-and-flares/\">solar activity</a>, <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/johnson/halloween-aboard-the-international-space-station/\">geomagnetic storms</a> have unleashed energetic particles trapped in Earth's magnetic field. Penetrating the planet's upper atmosphere at high latitudes, the particles create <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/sun/auroras/\">auroral displays</a> in the starry night sky. Ghostly towers of steam and gas are venting from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oWjdXf67dLQ\">local fumaroles to dance</a> against the eerie, greenish northern lights. For now, auroral activity on planet Earth remains in a high state as the Sun is only in early phases of decline from the peak of its <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_maximum\">solar activity cycle</a>. And soon, other ghostly apparitions may dance in your neighborhood. <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/johnson/halloween-aboard-the-international-space-station/\">Happy Halloween</a>!<br><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture: </strong><a href=\"///Users/jtbonnel/Desktop/apodT/ap261101.html\">Sunday's Childe</a>", "credit": "<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/stephane.vetter.nuitsacrees\">St\u00e9phane Vetter</a> (<a href=\"http://www.nuitsacrees.fr/\">Nuits sacr\u00e9es</a>)", "copyright": "<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/stephane.vetter.nuitsacrees\">St\u00e9phane Vetter</a> (<a href=\"http://www.nuitsacrees.fr/\">Nuits sacr\u00e9es</a>)", "alt": "Steam is venting from volcanic fumaroles photographed against greenish aurorae.", "url": "https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-31-night-on-a-spooky-planet/", "hdurl": "https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg?w=1300&h=867&fit=clip&crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint", "basic_html": "<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title> APOD: 2026 October 31 - Night on a Spooky Planet</title>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-31-night-on-a-spooky-planet/\">\n<!-- gsfc meta tags -->\n<meta name=\"orgcode\" content=\"661\">\n<meta name=\"rno\" content=\"Dana Bolles\">\n<meta name=\"content-owner\" content=\"Robert Nemiroff\">\n<meta name=\"webmaster\" content=\"Stephen.F.Fantasia.1\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Explanation: What spooky planet is this? Planet Earth on a dark and stormy night, of course. The ghostly scene was photographed at Hverir, a geothermally active area found along northeastern Iceland&#039;s volcanic landscape. Triggered by solar activity, geomagnetic storms have unleashed energetic particles trapped in Earth&#039;s magnetic field. Penetrating the planet&#039;s upper atmosphere at high latitudes, the particles create auroral displays in the starry night sky. Ghostly towers of steam and gas are venting from local fumaroles to dance against the eerie, greenish northern lights. For now, auroral activity on planet Earth remains in a high state as the Sun is only in early phases of decline from the peak of its solar activity cycle. And soon, other ghostly apparitions may dance in your neighborhood. Happy Halloween!Tomorrow&#039;s picture: Sunday&#039;s Childe\">\n<!-- -->\n<meta name=\"keywords\" content=\"night on a spooky planet\">\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\">\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Night on a Spooky Planet\">\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-31-night-on-a-spooky-planet/\">\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"NASA Science\">\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg?w=1300&#038;h=867&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:secure_url\" content=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg?w=1300&#038;h=867&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\">\n<meta property=\"og:image:alt\" content=\"Steam is venting from volcanic fumaroles photographed against greenish aurorae.\">\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2026-10-31T00:05:00-04:00\">\n<meta property=\"article:modified_time\" content=\"2026-10-30T12:16:26-04:00\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"Night on a Spooky Planet\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@NASA\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:creator\" content=\"@NASA\">\n<meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg?w=1300&#038;h=867&#038;fit=clip&#038;crop=faces%2Cfocalpoint\">\n</head>\n<body BGCOLOR=\"#F4F4FF\" text=\"#000000\" link=\"#0000FF\" vlink=\"#7F0F9F\"\nalink=\"#FF0000\">\n\n<center>\n<h1> Astronomy Picture of the Day </h1>\n<p>\n\n<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Discover the cosmos!</a>\nEach day a different image or photograph of our fascinating universe is\nfeatured, along with a brief explanation written by a professional astronomer.\n<p>\n\n2026 October 31<br>\n\n<a href=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg\">\n<IMG SRC=\"https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/cds/apod/apod/Hverir_Vetter_1300.jpg\" alt=\"Steam is venting from volcanic fumaroles photographed against greenish aurorae.\"></a>\n</center>\n\n<center>\n<b> Night on a Spooky Planet </b> <br>\n\n<b>Image Credit &\n<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/about-apod/\">Copyright</a>:</b>\n\n<a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/stephane.vetter.nuitsacrees\">St\u00e9phane Vetter</a> (<a href=\"http://www.nuitsacrees.fr/\">Nuits sacr\u00e9es</a>)\n</center>\n\n<p>\n\n<b> Explanation: </b>\n\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/solar-system/sinister-solar-system/\">What spooky planet is this?</a> Planet Earth on a dark and stormy night, of course. The ghostly scene was <a href=\"https://twanight.org/gallery/night-on-a-spooky-planet/\">photographed at Hverir</a>, a geothermally active area found along northeastern Iceland's <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Krafla\">volcanic landscape</a>. Triggered by <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/sun/solar-storms-and-flares/\">solar activity</a>, <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/johnson/halloween-aboard-the-international-space-station/\">geomagnetic storms</a> have unleashed energetic particles trapped in Earth's magnetic field. Penetrating the planet's upper atmosphere at high latitudes, the particles create <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/sun/auroras/\">auroral displays</a> in the starry night sky. Ghostly towers of steam and gas are venting from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=oWjdXf67dLQ\">local fumaroles to dance</a> against the eerie, greenish northern lights. For now, auroral activity on planet Earth remains in a high state as the Sun is only in early phases of decline from the peak of its <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_maximum\">solar activity cycle</a>. And soon, other ghostly apparitions may dance in your neighborhood. <a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/centers-and-facilities/johnson/halloween-aboard-the-international-space-station/\">Happy Halloween</a>!<br><br><strong>Tomorrow's picture: </strong><a href=\"///Users/jtbonnel/Desktop/apodT/ap261101.html\">Sunday's Childe</a>\n<p> <center>\n\n\n<p> <hr>\n<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/image-article/apod-2026-october-30-haunting-the-cepheus-flare/\">&lt;</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Archive</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Index</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/archive/\">Search</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/calendar/\">Calendar</a>\n| <a href=\"/feed/apod-basic/\">RSS</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/education-links/\">Education</a>\n| <a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/about-apod/\">About APOD</a>\n| &gt;\n\n<hr><p>\n<b> Authors & editors: </b>\nJerry Bonnell, Cecilia Chirenti, Robert Nemiroff, Keighley Rockcliffe<br>\n<b>NASA Official: </b> Dana Bolles<a href=\"https://science.nasa.gov/apod/about-apod/\">Specific rights apply</a>.<br>\n<a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/about/highlights/HP_Privacy.html\">NASA Web\nPrivacy Policy and Important Notices</a><br>\n<b>A service of:</b>\n<a href=\"http://astrophysics.gsfc.nasa.gov/\">ASD</a> at\n<a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/\">NASA</a> /\n<a href=\"http://www.nasa.gov/centers/goddard/\">GSFC</a>\n<br><b>&</b> <a href=\"http://www.mtu.edu/\">Michigan Tech. U.</a><br>\n</center>\n</body>\n</html>", "basic_html_url": "https://science.nasa.gov/wp-json/wp/v2/apod-basic/261031/html"}